-names>JG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Children with intellectual disability in rural South Africa : prevalence and associated disability.(Part 2)</article-title><source>Intellectual Disability Research</source><year>2002</year><volume>46</volume><fpage>179</fpage><lpage>186</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-2788.2002.00390.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Disler</surname><given-names>PB</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacks</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Sayed</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name><name><surname>Rip</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Hurford</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Collis</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The prevalence of  locomotor disability and handicap in the Cape Peninsula.  Part I. The coloured population of Bishop Lavis.</article-title><source>South African Medical Journal</source><year>1986</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>349</fpage><lpage>352</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2938278</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Disler</surname><given-names>PB</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacks</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Sayed</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name><name><surname>Rip</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Hurford</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Collis</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The prevalence of locomotor disability and handicap in the Cape Peninsula.  Part III. The white population of Fish Hoek</article-title><year>1986</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>355</fpage><lpage>357</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2938280</pub-id></citation></ref>